  "body": "Consider the following:\r\n```html\r\n<input id=myinput>\r\n<script>\r\nmyinput.onblur = () => console.log('blur event!');\r\nmyinput.focus();\r\nmyinput.remove();\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nShould `myinput` fire the `blur` event when it is removed?\r\nChrome fires the blur event, but Safari and Firefox do not.\r\nHere's a test page: https://jsfiddle.net/jarhar/eh4697d2/\r\n\r\nDue to similar logic with the `change` event, this behavior also occurs with the `change` event, which was raised here: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1297334\r\n\r\nI couldn't find anything in the DOM and HTML specs about this behavior.",
